---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/usgaap/asc845.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "General Measurement Principle — Fair Value" },
        { id: "s4", label: "The Commercial Substance Test — the Carryover Basis Exception" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Nonreciprocal Transfers" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example — an Exchange With Commercial Substance" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — an Exchange Lacking Commercial Substance" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s10", label: "ASC 845 vs IAS 16 — Comparison" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Related Topics" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Exchanges without cash — did economic substance actually change?</div><div class="principle">Most transactions involve cash or a monetary receivable/payable, making measurement straightforward. NONMONETARY transactions — exchanging one nonmonetary asset for another, or distributing nonmonetary assets to owners — raise a genuine question: has the entity's economic position actually CHANGED enough to justify recognising a gain or loss, or is this merely a continuation of the same underlying investment in a different form? ASC 845 answers this through the COMMERCIAL SUBSTANCE test (Section 4).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Exchanges and nonreciprocal transfers of nonmonetary assets</div><div class="principle">ASC 845 covers NONMONETARY EXCHANGES (trading one nonmonetary asset — e.g. property, inventory, equipment — for another) and NONRECIPROCAL TRANSFERS (distributing or receiving nonmonetary assets without an exchange, such as a dividend paid in the form of property rather than cash).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>General Measurement Principle — Fair Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Recorded at fair value, with gain/loss recognised</div><div class="principle">As a GENERAL rule, nonmonetary exchanges are measured at the FAIR VALUE of the asset(s) GIVEN UP (or the asset(s) RECEIVED, if that fair value is MORE CLEARLY EVIDENT) — with any difference between fair value and the asset's CARRYING amount recognised as a GAIN or LOSS. This treats the exchange as if the entity effectively SOLD the old asset at fair value and then PURCHASED the new one.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>The Commercial Substance Test — the Carryover Basis Exception</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">No genuine change in economic position, no gain recognised</div><div class="principle">If an exchange LACKS "commercial substance" — meaning the entity's FUTURE CASH FLOWS are NOT expected to change significantly as a result of the exchange — the transaction is instead recorded at the CARRYOVER (existing carrying amount) basis of the asset given up, with <strong>NO gain recognised</strong> (a loss would still generally be recognised, consistent with the conservatism inherent in impairment principles). A transaction generally has commercial substance if the RISK, TIMING, or AMOUNT of the entity's future cash flows is expected to change meaningfully as a result. This carryover-basis exception prevents entities from generating artificial "gains" simply by swapping economically similar assets.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Nonreciprocal Transfers</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Dividends in kind and contributions</div><div class="principle">A NONRECIPROCAL transfer — such as a dividend distributed to shareholders in the form of nonmonetary property, rather than cash — is generally measured at the FAIR VALUE of the asset transferred, with a GAIN OR LOSS recognised for the difference between fair value and the asset's carrying amount at the distribution date, similar in spirit to a sale followed by a distribution of the proceeds.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Worked Example — an Exchange With Commercial Substance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognising a gain</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Trading a delivery truck for a forklift</div><div class="wk-body">An entity exchanges a delivery truck (carrying amount $30,000, fair value $45,000) for a forklift used in a different part of its operations with materially different cash flow characteristics (fair value also $45,000). The exchange is expected to meaningfully change the timing and amount of the entity's future cash flows.</div><div class="wk-answer">Since the exchange HAS commercial substance, the truck is treated as effectively SOLD at its $45,000 fair value: recognise a GAIN of $45,000 − $30,000 = <strong>$15,000</strong>. The forklift is recorded at its $45,000 fair value.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — an Exchange Lacking Commercial Substance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Carryover basis, no gain recognised</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Swapping similar inventory between distributors</div><div class="wk-body">Two beverage distributors, each facing a temporary local shortage, swap similar quantities of the same product in different markets to meet customer demand — the swap has no expected effect on either entity's future cash flows, since each simply continues selling the same product at the same margins.</div><div class="wk-answer">Since the exchange LACKS commercial substance, the inventory received is recorded at the CARRYOVER (existing carrying amount) basis of the inventory given up — <strong>NO gain is recognised</strong>, even if the exchanged quantities happen to have differing fair values.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASC 845 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature of nonmonetary transactions, the basis of accounting for assets transferred, and gains/losses recognised</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Critical Judgments & Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
      <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether an exchange has commercial substance, i.e. whether future cash flows are expected to change significantly</span></div></div>
      <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of the nonmonetary assets exchanged, where not otherwise readily determinable</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>ASC 845 vs IAS 16 — Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASC 845 vs IAS 16's exchange of assets guidance</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">US GAAP (ASC 845)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS (IAS 16)</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>General measurement basis</span><span>Fair value, gain/loss recognised</span><span>Fair value, gain/loss recognised — converged</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Commercial substance exception</span><span>Carryover basis if lacking commercial substance</span><span>Same broad commercial substance test and carryover-basis exception — converged core concept</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">The core "commercial substance" test and its carryover-basis consequence are broadly CONVERGED between the two frameworks — this is one of the narrower Topics where the general principle travels well across both sets of standards.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every ASC 845 event lands</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Exchange with commercial substance</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Gain/loss recognised, new asset at fair value</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Exchange lacking commercial substance</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Carryover basis, no gain recognised</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Related Topics</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Topic</span><span>Connection</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 360</span><span>Property, Plant &amp; Equipment — supplies the carrying amount basis used in nonmonetary exchange gain/loss calculations</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 820</span><span>Supplies the fair value measurement framework applied when fair value must be determined</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Commercial substance</div><div class="glossary-def">A determination of whether an entity's future cash flows are expected to change significantly as a result of a nonmonetary exchange.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Nonreciprocal transfer</div><div class="glossary-def">A one-directional transfer of nonmonetary assets, such as a dividend distributed in kind, without an exchange in return.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Carryover basis</div><div class="glossary-def">Recording an asset received in an exchange at the existing carrying amount of the asset given up, used when the exchange lacks commercial substance.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.ASC845 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
